title: Authorizations › New case › Referral › Check coverage
route: /authorizations/new/:draftId?ref=RF-2053 (checklist) and /authorizations/new/referral/RF-2053 (Coverage tab)
intro: Verify can check a referral's coverage from the checklist row or from the Coverage tab on the full page. For the full check, the Coverage tab hands off to Eligibility & Benefits.
dir: TD
also: Demo only: Verify's answer is fixed for each referral (covered, authorization first, lapsed, or no insurance) and takes about three seconds.
---
start s1 "Checklist, Coverage section:\n'Verify checked coverage' row"
start s2 "Full page: open the 'Coverage' tab"

decision d1 "Does the referral list an insurance?"
process p1 "Row says 'Optional'\n'Verify needs the insurance and member ID first.'\nNo button"
goto g1 "Continues in: New case › Referral › Ask the referrer"
process p2 "Row says 'Optional'\n'Not checked yet. Verify looks up eligibility, the plan and whether an authorization is needed first.'"
click c1 "Click 'Run coverage check'"

group gTab "Coverage tab"
  screen sc1 "Card 'Coverage has not been checked'\n'Verify looks up eligibility, the plan, the authorization rule and the program's network status.'"
  process p3 "No insurance on the referral:\n'Verify will report that it cannot confirm coverage'"
  click c2 "Click 'Run coverage check'"
  overlay o1 "Card 'Verify is checking coverage'\n'This takes a few seconds.'\nEligibility with Summit · Benefits and plan · Authorization rule and network status"
endgroup

store st0 "Verify is running for this referral\nRow shows 'Verify is checking coverage.' with a spinner"
agent a1 "Verify checks eligibility, benefits and plan,\nauthorization rule and network status"
decision d2 "What does Verify find?"
store st1 "Coverage saved on the referral\nTimeline 'Verify checked coverage: …'"
toast t1 "'Verify checked coverage'\n'Covered and ready to admit'"
toast t2 "'Verify checked coverage'\n'Covered, but you need an authorization first'"
toast t3 "Amber toast 'Verify checked coverage'\n'Coverage has lapsed. Fix this before billing'"
process p4 "Checklist row turns Done\nProgress changes from 11 to 12 items"
process p5 "Row turns 'Check this' with 'Check again'\nRed banner on the full page 'Verify found that coverage has lapsed' with 'Open coverage'"
screen sc2 "Coverage tab result\nBanner with the headline, 'Check again'\nCard 'Payment checks' with six lines and 'Checked live at 10:42 am'"
click c3 "Click 'Check again'"

click c4 "Click 'Open full Eligibility & Benefits check'"
process p6 "Opens Verify a patient with the referral's payer,\nmember ID, level of care and a made-up birth date filled in"
goto g2 "Continues in: Eligibility & Benefits › Verify a patient"
start s3 "Coming back: 'Start authorization'\non the coverage result (authorization first)"
process p7 "Opens a NEW case with payer, level of care, member ID, initials and age\nIt is not tied to the referral or its case"
goto g3 "Continues in: New case › How a case starts and resumes"
start s4 "Press the browser Back button\non Verify a patient or its result"
process p8 "Returns to the referral page\nNo button in Eligibility leads back to the referral"

s1 --> d1
d1 -->|No| p1 --> g1
d1 -->|Yes| p2 --> c1
c1 --> st0
s2 --> sc1
sc1 -.-> p3
sc1 --> c2 --> st0
st0 --> o1
st0 --> a1 --> d2
d2 -->|Covered| st1
d2 -->|Authorization first| st1
d2 -->|Lapsed| st1
st1 --> t1 --> p4
st1 --> t2 --> p4
st1 --> t3 --> p5
p4 --> sc2
p5 --> sc2
p5 --> c3 --> st0
sc2 --> c3
sc2 --> c4 --> p6 --> g2
s4 --> p8 --> sc2
s3 --> p7 --> g3
